# Migration iteration 4 — WP-10 Increment T: tie-pin trace shape reduction (2026-10-06)

Goal (from handoff): port `ShapeSearchTree::reduce_trace_shape_at_tie_pin` +
`change_item_shape`, wire `MazeSearchAlgo::init`, tests, build, run, update tracking.

## Baseline
- `cmake --build build` OK, `ctest` 745/745, `./build/tests/data/run_tests` All PASSED.

## Code (all Java-parity, Java = ShapeSearchTree.java:922-1010, MazeSearchEngine.java:970-971)
- `src/board/Item.h/.cpp`: new public `get_precalculated_tree_shapes(const ShapeTree&)` and
  `set_precalculated_tree_shapes(vector<shared_ptr<TileShape>>, const ShapeTree&)` (lazy-create
  `search_trees_info_`, mirror of `take`/`set_search_tree_entries`).
- `src/board/ShapeSearchTree.h/.cpp`: `change_item_shape(Item*, int, shared_ptr<TileShape>)`
  (take entries → index guard with warn → `ShapeTree::remove({old leaf})` → replace
  precalculated shape → rebuild entries → `ShapeTree::insert(*p_item, p_shape_index)` →
  `set_search_tree_entries`) and `reduce_trace_shape_at_tie_pin(Pin*, PolylineTrace*)`
  (pin shape on trace layer → first/last corner == pin center → shape 0 / corner_count()-2 →
  2-D intersection guard → `cutout` pieces → first 2-D piece or piece containing compare corner →
  `change_item_shape`). Placed before `ShapeSearchTree::clear()`.
- `src/autoroute/MazeSearchAlgo.cpp`: anonymous-namespace
  `reduce_trace_shapes_at_tie_pins(set<Item*>, net_no, search_tree*)` (Pin + net_count>1 →
  normal contacts → PolylineTrace not containing own net → reduce), called for start AND dest
  lists at the top of `init`, replacing the divergence comment.

## Tests (registered in tests/CMakeLists.txt)
- NEW `src/board/ShapeSearchTree_tie_pin_test.cpp` — 7 gtests: change replaces shape + keeps
  tree consistent (size/overlap/validate_entries), out-of-range no-op, first-corner reduction,
  last-corner reduction of a 3-corner trace (first shape untouched), no corner at pin no-op,
  pin layer mismatch no-op, null args.
  - Fix during bring-up: FloatPoint lives in `geometry/planar/Point.h` (no FloatPoint.h);
    tree size assertion must count the pin leaf too (2, not 1).
- `MazeSearchAlgoTest.InitReducesForeignTraceShapesAtTiePins` — foreign {2} trace reduced
  (pin center gone, far corner survives), own {1} trace untouched, entries valid.

## Verification
- `ctest --test-dir build`: **753/753 passed** (745 + 7 + 1).
- `./build/tests/data/run_tests`: **All tests PASSED**.

## Discovered latent bug (NOT on this path, NOT fixed)
- `TileShape::cutout` (`src/geometry/planar/TileShape.cpp` ~line 794): the two branches where
  the hole is a `Simplex` and the divider is `IntOctagon`/`IntBox` call
  `divide->cutout_from(hole)` → returns hole-minus-divide (inverted vs Java A.cutout(B) =
  A minus B). Tie-pin only uses octagon/octagon (correct). Recorded in
  `SOURCE_OF_TRUTH/03_MISSING.md` §2.1, `MIGRATION_board.md`, `05_WORK_PACKAGES.md` Inc T.

